[00:00.00] 作曲 : Ian Christian/Jordan Fletcher
[00:10.79] Guitars, trucks and cowboy boots
[00:10.79] 吉他 卡车与牛仔靴
[00:13.63] A few things better used
[00:13.63] 有些事物愈久愈珍
[00:15.95] When you can see what they've been through, you know they're made to last
[00:15.95] 当见证岁月痕迹 便知它们为永恒而生
[00:21.32] There's nothing wrong with faded jeans
[00:21.32] 褪色牛仔并无不妥
[00:24.13] Couple tears, frayed seams
[00:24.13] 破洞缝线 磨损边缘
[00:26.79] Baby, all that really means is that we all got a past
[00:26.79] 亲爱的 这不过印证 世人皆有往事沉淀
[00:31.27]
[00:31.32] I don't trust a horse that ain't been rode
[00:31.32] 我不信未驯服的野马
[00:35.08] Or a truck that ain't been sold
[00:35.08] 或未转手的崭新皮卡
[00:37.48] Hands and hearts that ain't got scars, they ain't worth holding
[00:37.48] 无疤的手掌与心脏 不值得紧握珍藏
[00:42.72] Songs sound better on rusty strings
[00:42.72] 生锈琴弦更显声韵
[00:45.52] Worn-in leather feels good to me
[00:45.52] 磨旧皮革最称我意
[00:47.82] Guess you could say that I like things
[00:47.82] 或许你会说 我偏爱
[00:51.42] Broken, broken in
[00:51.42] 历经沧桑的 沉淀时光的
[00:58.11] Broken in
[00:58.11] 岁月印记
[01:00.25]
[01:04.04] Say all that to tell the truth
[01:04.04] 坦言相告皆为真意
[01:06.64] There's still some things that I like new
[01:06.64] 仍有新物令我倾心
[01:09.17] Like the first time that I kissed you
[01:09.17] 如初吻你的颤栗
[01:11.87] And the first smoke out of that pack
[01:11.87] 如新拆烟盒第一缕氤氲
[01:14.54] From who we are to where we've been
